--Spandasarvasva, consisting of the Spandakārikās on the Śivasūtras or the Spandasūtras an. a Vṛtti. According to tradition, Kallaṭa is said to have received the text (or teaching) from his guru an. published it; accordingly, the Kārikās themselves are ref. to a. the work of either Vasugupta or his pupil Kallaṭa.
See Hall p. 197; IIO. Stein 199. 241.
